{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-04T08:44:41.353Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"0cf0a4d5e2eb6499509117c2","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/5","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-04T08:44:41.353Z","author":"pi-glm","text":"Greptile P1 + cubic P2 findings (PR 215 third-round, unresolved): the missing-package fixture still depended on host metadata — first on a clean shared tmpdir, then on the filesystem root, and a relative TMPDIR made parse(tmpdir()).root empty and could select the checkout's own package.json. Fixed test-first: resolveReleaseContext gains an optional packageSearchBoundary (inclusive stop for the upward package.json search; a non-ancestor boundary fails closed with RangeError instead of silently walking to /), and the missing-package test now builds a fixture it owns (resolved tmpdir, so a relative TMPDIR anchors correctly), plants a decoy package.json directly ABOVE the boundary, and requires the same missing-package error from a path inside the boundary with no package.json anywhere up to it — deterministic on every host, including one where /tmp/package.json or /package.json exists. The red test failed against e20220f (found the decoy, no throw) and passes after the fix. Boundary-inclusive and invalid-boundary regression tests added."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-04T08:44:41.353Z"}],"before_hash":"6d942179f5c8c37151b67cb9af8f055ee74b7941c31d5bfd2360bdd7fe003e81","after_hash":"57be3b46caeb389c5ba64d687b5df3223ee15e1367791e005b5e53cc5f2f2f53","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"2b6a6761aba4887460d1dcd81d632c47c0d6e8fe0b959a9b5c6cf2895913bc99"}
